    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "This study establishes a theoretical framework for constructing functional connectivity networks to model delay propagation in transportation systems, detailing common pitfalls in correlation and causality testing. Another paper applies a relational egalitarianism framework to analyze transport injustice in the medium-sized Indian city of Siliguri, drawing on interviews with institutional stakeholders, slum-dwelling households, and shop owners near railway stations. Finally, a third study evaluated environmental health literacy among 205 urban cyclists in Ljubljana, Slovenia, who participated in a two-week citizen science project using personal PM2.5 and noise sensors alongside a custom visualization platform.",
